#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:1
msgid ""
"Can I cache this? [![Build Status](https://travis-ci.org/pornel/http-"
"cache-semantics.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.org/pornel/http-"
"cache-semantics)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:1
msgid "Build Status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:3
msgid ""
"`CachePolicy` tells when responses can be reused from a cache, taking "
"into account [HTTP RFC 7234](http://httpwg.org/specs/rfc7234.html) rules "
"for user agents and shared caches. It's aware of many tricky details such"
" as the `Vary` header, proxy revalidation, and authenticated responses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:5
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:7
msgid ""
"Cacheability of an HTTP response depends on how it was requested, so both"
" `request` and `response` are required to create the policy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:35
msgid ""
"It may be surprising, but it's not enough for an HTTP response to be "
"[fresh](#yo-fresh) to satisfy a request. It may need to match request "
"headers specified in `Vary`. Even a matching fresh response may still not"
" be usable if the new request restricted cacheability, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:37
msgid ""
"The key method is `satisfiesWithoutRevalidation(newRequest)`, which "
"checks whether the `newRequest` is compatible with the original request "
"and whether all caching conditions are met."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:39
msgid "Constructor options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:41
msgid ""
"Request and response must have a `headers` property with all header names"
" in lower case. `url`, `status` and `method` are optional (defaults are "
"any URL, status `200`, and `GET` method)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:67
msgid ""
"If `options.shared` is `true` (default), then the response is evaluated "
"from a perspective of a shared cache (i.e. `private` is not cacheable and"
" `s-maxage` is respected). If `options.shared` is `false`, then the "
"response is evaluated from a perspective of a single-user cache (i.e. "
"`private` is cacheable and `s-maxage` is ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:69
msgid ""
"`options.cacheHeuristic` is a fraction of response's age that is used as "
"a fallback cache duration. The default is 0.1 (10%), e.g. if a file "
"hasn't been modified for 100 days, it'll be cached for 100*0.1 = 10 days."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:71
msgid ""
"`options.immutableMinTimeToLive` is a number of milliseconds to assume as"
" the default time to cache responses with `Cache-Control: immutable`. "
"Note that [per RFC](http://httpwg.org/http-extensions/immutable.html) "
"these can become stale, so `max-age` still overrides the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:73
msgid ""
"If `options.ignoreCargoCult` is true, common anti-cache directives will "
"be completely ignored if the non-standard `pre-check` and `post-check` "
"directives are present. These two useless directives are most commonly "
"found in bad StackOverflow answers and PHP's \"session limiter\" "
"defaults."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:75
msgid "`storable()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:77
msgid ""
"Returns `true` if the response can be stored in a cache. If it's `false` "
"then you MUST NOT store either the request or the response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:79
msgid "`satisfiesWithoutRevalidation(newRequest)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:81
msgid ""
"This is the most important method. Use this method to check whether the "
"cached response is still fresh in the context of the new request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:83
msgid ""
"If it returns `true`, then the given `request` matches the original "
"response this cache policy has been created with, and the response can be"
" reused without contacting the server. Note that the old response can't "
"be returned without being updated, see `responseHeaders()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:85
msgid ""
"If it returns `false`, then the response may not be matching at all (e.g."
" it's for a different URL or method), or may require to be refreshed "
"first (see `revalidationHeaders()`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:87
msgid "`responseHeaders()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:89
msgid ""
"Returns updated, filtered set of response headers to return to clients "
"receiving the cached response. This function is necessary, because "
"proxies MUST always remove hop-by-hop headers (such as `TE` and "
"`Connection`) and update response's `Age` to avoid doubling cache time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:95
msgid "`timeToLive()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:97
msgid ""
"Returns approximate time in *milliseconds* until the response becomes "
"stale (i.e. not fresh)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:99
msgid ""
"After that time (when `timeToLive() <= 0`) the response might not be "
"usable without revalidation. However, there are exceptions, e.g. a client"
" can explicitly allow stale responses, so always check with "
"`satisfiesWithoutRevalidation()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:101
msgid "`toObject()`/`fromObject(json)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:103
msgid ""
"Chances are you'll want to store the `CachePolicy` object along with the "
"cached response. `obj = policy.toObject()` gives a plain JSON-"
"serializable object. `policy = CachePolicy.fromObject(obj)` creates an "
"instance from it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:105
msgid "Refreshing stale cache (revalidation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:107
msgid ""
"When a cached response has expired, it can be made fresh again by making "
"a request to the origin server. The server may respond with status 304 "
"(Not Modified) without sending the response body again, saving bandwidth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:109
msgid "The following methods help perform the update efficiently and correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:111
msgid "`revalidationHeaders(newRequest)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:113
msgid ""
"Returns updated, filtered set of request headers to send to the origin "
"server to check if the cached response can be reused. These headers allow"
" the origin server to return status 304 indicating the response is still "
"fresh. All headers unrelated to caching are passed through as-is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:115
msgid "Use this method when updating cache from the origin server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:121
msgid "`revalidatedPolicy(revalidationRequest, revalidationResponse)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:123
msgid ""
"Use this method to update the cache after receiving a new response from "
"the origin server. It returns an object with two keys:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:125
msgid ""
"`policy` — A new `CachePolicy` with HTTP headers updated from "
"`revalidationResponse`. You can always replace the old cached "
"`CachePolicy` with the new one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:126
msgid "`modified` — Boolean indicating whether the response body has changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:127
msgid ""
"If `false`, then a valid 304 Not Modified response has been received, and"
" you can reuse the old cached response body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-cache-semantics_README.md:128
msgid ""
"If `true`, you should use new response's body (if present), or make "
"another request to the origin server without any conditional headers "
"(i.e. don't use `revalidationHeaders()` this time) to get the new "
"resource."
msgstr ""

